{
  "about": "Module and dependency map of the Rust MnemoCode (docs/design/architect/ARCHITECTURE.md sections 2 and 3), read by the code-rules gate (cargo xtask code-rules). layers: a library module may use the foundation and the modules listed for it ('*': every module); a module of mnemocode-cards or mnemocode-cli uses only the modules before it in 'order'; every listed edge of an existing library module is used. deps: each crate's direct dependencies per target, its devDependencies for its tests, and refusedInTree for every artifact. unsafe: 'forbid' in the crate root, or 'deny' with allow(unsafe_code) only in the files and folders of allowedIn (paths relative to the crate, a folder ending in /). ioModules: the only CLI files and folders whose top may expect clippy's disallowed std methods and types, besides test modules and integration test files.",
